## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical integration of real-time data streams, memoization strategies, and optimistic UI patterns within multi-tenant architectures.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant useSyncExternalStore streams
- Memoized selectors keyed by (tenantId, notificationId)
- React.memo for individual notification items
- react-window virtualization for performance
- Optimistic UI updates with rollback capability
- Cleanup on tenant switch and reconnection handling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Per-tenant store wrapper
const createTenantNotificationStore = (tenantId) => {
  const subscribers = new Set();
  let notifications = [];

  return {
    subscribe: (callback) => {
      subscribers.add(callback);
      return () => subscribers.delete(callback);
    },
    getSnapshot: () => notifications,
    getServerSnapshot: () => [],
  };
};

// Memoized selector
const createNotificationSelector = (tenantId, notificationId) => {
  return createSelector(
    [selectNotificationsByTenant(tenantId)],
    (notifications) => notifications.find(n => n.id === notificationId)
  );
};
```

